WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:01.052
- We are back.

00:00:01.052 --> 00:00:02.551
Kal Penn is here with us,

00:00:02.551 --> 00:00:03.384
y'all give it up!

00:00:03.384 --> 00:00:05.549
(audience cheering)

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:07.947
His new book is called
"You Can't Be Serious"

00:00:07.947 --> 00:00:09.360
and it's out now.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.193
You've got to check it out.

00:00:10.193 --> 00:00:11.890
So where does the title
of the book come from?

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:12.830
It's awesome.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.480
- I wanted a title, that captures

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.970
basically a double entendre in,

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.440
you know, when I decided
I want to be an actor.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.685
My guidance counselor said,

00:00:20.685 --> 00:00:21.518
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:21.518 --> 00:00:22.351
she said...

00:00:22.351 --> 00:00:23.310
oh, I said, "I want to be an actor

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.140
and then I want to do
something in public service."

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.328
And she said, "You can't have
your cake and eat it too."

00:00:27.328 --> 00:00:28.161
And I was like, really-

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:28.994
- [Kelly] Oh I hate those people.

00:00:28.994 --> 00:00:30.090
- Like, as a 16 year old,

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.030
you're going to tell me that nope,

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.050
you're life possibilities-

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.259
- Your dream-
- [Kal] Come on!

00:00:34.259 --> 00:00:35.092
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:00:35.092 --> 00:00:35.925
There's a limit to your dreams.

00:00:35.925 --> 00:00:36.881
- [Kal] Right.

00:00:36.881 --> 00:00:38.060
So there was that and then when I,

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.080
you know, post, like done
a bunch of stoner movies

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.680
and played a doctor on TV and all of this.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.513
- Love those.

00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:43.346
(audience cheers)

00:00:43.346 --> 00:00:44.179
- [Kal] Thank you, I love them too.

00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:45.012
- Yes, Yes, Yes.

00:00:45.012 --> 00:00:45.845
(audience cheers)

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.730
- But go off to work at The White House.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.110
And it's a similar thing.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:50.950
Oh, you're crazy.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.783
Why would you do that?

00:00:51.783 --> 00:00:52.616
You can't do that.

00:00:52.616 --> 00:00:54.280
You're known for playing a stoner.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.900
And, but the only people
who really focused on that

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:57.980
were journalists, you know?
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.844
- 'Cause they're trying to
get like the clickbait thing-

00:00:59.844 --> 00:01:00.680
- [Kelly] 'Cause they just
want a clickbait story.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.513
- Exactly.
- Yeah, it's unfortunate.

00:01:01.513 --> 00:01:02.840
And I get that that's their gig.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:03.930
But the title of the book-

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.590
- I don't. That's not real journalism.

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:06.570
- [Kal] Its not.
- Yeah.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:07.470
And I said it.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:08.380
There, it's out there.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.213
Yeah.

00:01:10.082 --> 00:01:10.915
(audience cheers)

00:01:10.915 --> 00:01:12.040
- So the title of the book,

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.900
I wanted it to be a play
on both of those things

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:15.733
that you know-
- Yeah.

00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:16.950
- That you can't be serious,
but you actually can.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.070
There's a time to be serious

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.460
and there's a time to be
completely ridiculous.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.280
- And what a horrible thing
for a guidance counselor,

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.354
whatever they say like-
- [Kal] Yeah.

00:01:22.354 --> 00:01:23.187
Well she's dead now.

00:01:23.187 --> 00:01:25.854
(laughs loudly)

00:01:26.969 --> 00:01:28.046
- So wait, is it?

00:01:28.046 --> 00:01:30.624
This is perhaps my
favorite thing in the book.

00:01:30.624 --> 00:01:31.457
(laughs)

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:33.350
Is it true that you
almost took The President

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.183
to a strip club?

00:01:34.183 --> 00:01:35.231
- All right.

00:01:35.231 --> 00:01:37.280
(laughs loudly)

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.880
- It's a stretch to say almost took

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.720
but I did commit

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.090
and here's what happened.

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.670
It was my second week there,

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:48.741
third week there, right.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:49.574
(laughs loudly)

00:01:49.574 --> 00:01:50.407
I'm new to DC.

00:01:50.407 --> 00:01:51.430
I needed a haircut

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.930
and I just went to the
closest place to my apartment

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.430
right outside of Dupont Circle in D.C.

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:57.580
And this guy Rudolfo, who's the barber

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.600
and he recognized me

00:01:58.600 --> 00:01:59.520
and said, "I love your movies.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.750
I heard that you're working
at The White House."

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.030
And just talks my ear off.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.460
And I'm looking at my BlackBerry

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.590
trying to do work emails

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.530
while he's cutting my hair

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:06.910
and also trying to be nice.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.930
And he says, "You know, I own a tapas bar

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.050
that you should check out."

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:12.229
And I said-

00:02:12.229 --> 00:02:13.062
- I love tapas.

00:02:13.062 --> 00:02:13.895
- Me too.

00:02:13.895 --> 00:02:14.728
(audience laughing)

00:02:14.728 --> 00:02:15.561
I was getting hungry,

00:02:15.561 --> 00:02:16.550
so I said, "That's great."

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:19.020
And he said, "You should
actually bring your office,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.260
The White House Office
of Public Engagement

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.110
to my tapas bar."

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.680
And I was like, "Oh, sure. I mean maybe."

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.360
And then I think you all
know where this is going.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.193
- Oh my god.

00:02:27.193 --> 00:02:28.487
- And then he says,

00:02:28.487 --> 00:02:30.648
"Well, you should bring
The President too."

00:02:30.648 --> 00:02:31.481
(audience laughing)

00:02:31.481 --> 00:02:33.180
And people would say
those things all the time.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.400
And then he said, "You know,
it's all on the house."

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.233
And I said, "You know,

00:02:36.233 --> 00:02:38.180
there are a lot of ethics
rules at The Obama White House.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.890
We can't accept free anything.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.100
Why don't you give me your card?

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.190
And maybe I can bring
everybody for a holiday party

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:45.670
or something and we'll rent out your bar."

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:46.630
So he gives me his card.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:48.997
I put them in my pocket.
- Tapas bar? (laughs)

00:02:48.997 --> 00:02:49.970
- I get home.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.930
I put my phone, wallet, keys on my desk.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.060
I'm like, "Oh yeah, this dude's card."

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:53.893
And I look at it.

00:02:53.893 --> 00:02:56.926
It says "Rudolfo's ladies topless bar".

00:02:56.926 --> 00:02:57.900
(audience laughs)

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.661
- Which is amazing.

00:02:59.661 --> 00:03:01.222
(audience clapping)

00:03:01.222 --> 00:03:03.580
- And I was like-
- Which is amazing!

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.100
- So I had to go in the next day,

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.170
tell my boss what I did

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.030
because I could only imagine

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.789
that the Politico or TMZ story was

00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:11.622
(Kelly gasps)

00:03:11.622 --> 00:03:12.823
Kumar promises like

00:03:12.823 --> 00:03:13.656
(laughs loudly)

00:03:13.656 --> 00:03:16.080
strip club experience
for White House staff.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.330
- Who is bringing the ones?

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.337
- Right, yeah.

00:03:18.337 --> 00:03:19.170
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.003
It was fine.

00:03:20.003 --> 00:03:21.854
And he was very gracious and
nothing ever came of that.

00:03:21.854 --> 00:03:22.687
- [Kelly] Oh my god!

00:03:22.687 --> 00:03:23.665
- Yeah, it definitely
put my foot in my mouth.

00:03:23.665 --> 00:03:24.498
- No, yeah.

00:03:24.498 --> 00:03:25.490
Second weekend too.
- Second weekend.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.380
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:27.791
- Way to leave some footprints.

00:03:27.791 --> 00:03:29.607
- I do need to say that...

00:03:29.607 --> 00:03:30.440
(audience cheers)

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:31.273
- I tried,

00:03:31.273 --> 00:03:33.350
you were asking about the
title of the book before

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.450
and this is one of the things like

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:35.990
I tell that story for the first time.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.240
- And people are like,
"You can't be serious."

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.240
- And people say, "You can't be serious."

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.770
And then I also walk through
things like voter suppression

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.860
and outreach to young voters

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:43.900
and what it's like to register

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.210
in the history of our country.

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:47.290
I just love that people
have been responding

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.700
to both of those things

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.270
in the same kind of chapter.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.550
- I love that you have
all of that in one book.

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:53.690
What a great...

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:54.750
That's why it took four years

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.175
but I'm like just saying,

00:03:56.175 --> 00:03:57.300
it seems like it has a lot of heart,

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.960
has a lot of humor, has a lot of facts.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:00.793
- [Kal] Yeah.

00:04:00.793 --> 00:04:01.626
- And yeah, it's really...

00:04:01.626 --> 00:04:02.459
And you let walls down.

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:03.292
That's really cool.

00:04:03.292 --> 00:04:04.720
And you didn't need to
though, just so you know,

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.610
like I was a fan
regardless of who you like.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:08.443
- Thank you.

00:04:08.443 --> 00:04:09.276
(audience cheering)

00:04:09.276 --> 00:04:11.207
- Kal's book is called
"You Can't Be Serious"

00:04:11.207 --> 00:04:12.100
and it's out now.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.667
You've got to go check it out.

